# FoodRescue Network Documentation

## 1. Project Overview

### Project Title

**FoodRescue Network**

### Domain

Social Welfare / Food Waste Management

### Technology Stack

* MongoDB
* Express.js
* React.js
* Node.js
* Tailwind CSS
* Socket.io
* Leaflet Maps
* Nodemailer
* Twilio

### Project Description

FoodRescue Network is a full-stack MERN web application designed to reduce food waste by connecting food donors with NGOs and volunteers. The platform enables restaurants, grocery stores, and individuals to donate surplus food efficiently to people in need.

The system provides real-time communication, geolocation-based donation discovery, donation lifecycle tracking, and role-based access control for secure operations.

---

# 2. Objectives

* Reduce food wastage
* Help NGOs and volunteers access surplus food quickly
* Provide real-time food donation tracking
* Enable location-based food distribution
* Improve communication between donors and receivers

---

# 3. System Architecture

## Frontend

The frontend is developed using React 19 and Tailwind CSS.

### Features

* Responsive UI
* Interactive maps using Leaflet
* Real-time notifications using Socket.io-client
* Authentication management using Context API

## Backend

The backend is developed using Node.js and Express.js.

### Features

* RESTful APIs
* JWT Authentication
* Role-Based Access Control
* Notification services
* Business logic handling

## Database

MongoDB is used as the primary database.

### Features

* Mongoose ODM
* 2dsphere indexing for geolocation search
* Efficient document storage

